<spell-notebook "theme-editor theming">
	<header level="1">
		Theme Editor
		<header>A theme editor makes a theme from an existing one:  its colours, fonts and shapes, live on real elements, then copied as a stylesheet or kept in the browser.</>
	</>
	<theme-editor-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Set a public `--ui-*` token on the element, any ancestor or `:root`; it inherits into the shadow
			root. Edit a value below to try it.
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-theme-editor" playground>
				<ui-theme-editor></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
